# Selects which LlmProvider the worker builds. FAKE (the default) uses the
# deterministic FakeLlmProvider and makes no network call; LIVE uses
# ClaudeLlmProvider and makes real, billed Anthropic API calls.
#
# The execution mode is provider-neutral — there is no CLAUDE value. The vendor
# and model are expressed through model metadata, not through this enum, and
# FAKE | LIVE is what the database already persists as agent_runs.provider_mode.
#
# As of PR 6B1 apps/api can also execute a requested LIVE run, so live mode is no
# longer worker-only. There, this variable is the DEFAULT REQUEST MODE and a
# separate kill switch (LIVE_AGENT_RUNS_ENABLED, default false) gates live
# execution — see docs/12-agent-run-api.md §7.1. For this worker it keeps its
# original meaning: which provider the scripts below build.
AGENT_RUN_PROVIDER_MODE=FAKE

# Required ONLY when AGENT_RUN_PROVIDER_MODE=LIVE, and for the live spikes
# below. Never put a value here — .env is gitignored; this file is committed.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The only model this milestone supports. Validated at configuration time: any
# other value fails before a request is ever made, because the current request
# policy (thinking disabled alongside a forced tool_choice) is validated for
# claude-sonnet-5 only. Adding another model needs a capability-aware request
# policy and its own tests, not just a new pricing row.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional, LIVE only. Validated defaults are used if unset.
#
# ANTHROPIC_TIMEOUT_MS is the SDK's PER-ATTEMPT timeout, not a total budget:
# retry backoff and any retry-after delay add time on top of it, and a full
# agent run makes two provider calls. A caller-owned AbortSignal (the live smoke
# supplies a 120s one) bounds Anthropic provider calls across the run — tool,
# retrieval, and persistence cancellation are not wired in this milestone, so it
# is not a strict deadline for the entire run.
#
# The SDK is the sole retry owner — the application and orchestrator add none.
ANTHROPIC_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES=1

# Set to exactly "1" to authorize the paid live smoke
# (pnpm --filter @opspilot/worker run test:claude:live). Checked separately from
# AGENT_RUN_PROVIDER_MODE so an already-exported LIVE mode is never mistaken for
# an intent to spend money right now.
# OPSPILOT_LIVE_SMOKE=1

# Required only for the live RAG spike (pnpm run spike:rag).
VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# Optional for the live RAG spike — validated defaults are used if unset.
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS must be one of: 256, 512, 1024, 2048.
EMBEDDING_MODEL=voyage-4-lite
EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024

# Optional for the live RAG spike — selects which scenario(s) to run.
# RAG_SPIKE_SCENARIO must be one of: all, baseline, injection. Defaults to
# "all" if unset.
RAG_SPIKE_SCENARIO=all

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation scorer selection (OpsPilot #61 Phase 3)
#
# The evaluation CLI (pnpm --filter @opspilot/worker run eval) scores the
# normalized v1 suite either in-process ("local", the default) or against the
# Python/FastAPI evaluation service ("service"). Selection is explicit and
# fail-closed: an unrecognized EVALUATION_SCORER value is a configuration
# error. There is deliberately NO automatic fallback from "service" back to
# "local" — an unreachable service fails the evaluation (see
# service-unavailable.test.ts).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# EVALUATION_SCORER=local|service
#
# "local" (default when unset/empty) — LocalEvaluationScorer in-process.
# "service" — POSTs the same normalized v1 suite to the Python service; a
# malformed/unsupported response, timeout, or unreachable service fails the
# evaluation with a non-zero exit and no fabricated result.
EVALUATION_SCORER=local

# Required when EVALUATION_SCORER=service. Must be an absolute http(s) URL
# (e.g. the local dev service from services/evaluation: make migrate; make run).
# The client appends /evaluations (POST) and /evaluations/{id} (GET).
EVALUATION_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001

# Optional when EVALUATION_SCORER=service — a single bounded request timeout
# in milliseconds, clamped to [1000, 600000]; defaults to 15000 when unset.
# There are no retries in Phase 3; a timeout is a distinct failure category
# from "service unreachable".
EVALUATION_SERVICE_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
